## 6. Directory Structure

```text
private-llm-analytics/
├── configs/
│   ├── scenario.yaml
│   ├── privacy.yaml
│   ├── metrics.yaml
│   └── recipients.yaml
├── src/
│   └── private_llm_analytics/
│       ├── config/        # Pydantic models, YAML loaders & validators
│       ├── ingestion/     # Schema validation, CSV & Parquet loaders
│       ├── simulator/     # Heterogeneous employee preference simulator
│       ├── aggregation/   # Vectorized user-matrix aggregation & windows
│       ├── contribution/  # Binary, normalization & L2 clipping transforms
│       ├── mechanisms/    # Analytic Gaussian & Laplace DP mechanisms
│       ├── privacy/       # Budget, accountant, SQLite ledger & policies
│       ├── metrics/       # Prevalence, Normalized Share & Volume
│       ├── planner/       # Query planning & stable release key hashing
│       ├── release/       # Release cache, orchestrator & recipient filter
│       ├── evaluation/    # Ground truth, multi-trial harness & accuracy
│       └── service/       # Unified AnalyticsService facade
├── experiments/
│   ├── exp01_baseline.py
│   ├── exp02_epsilon.py
│   ├── exp03_population.py
│   └── exp04_clipping.py
├── data/                  # Synthetic Parquet datasets
├── results/
│   ├── raw/               # Trial-level CSV outputs
│   ├── tables/            # Summary experiment CSV tables
│   └── figures/           # Publication-ready PNG and PDF plots
├── tests/                 # Unit & correctness test suite
├── pyproject.toml
├── run_all_experiments.py
├── IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md
└── README.md
```

---

## 7. Installation & Quickstart

### Prerequisites
- Python 3.10+ (tested on Python 3.14)
- Packages: `numpy`, `scipy`, `pandas`, `pyarrow`, `pydantic`, `pyyaml`, `matplotlib`, `pytest`

### Installation
```bash
git clone <repo>
cd private-llm-analytics
pip install -e .
```

### Running Unit Tests
```bash
pytest tests/
```

### Running Experiments
```bash
# Run all experiments sequentially:
python run_all_experiments.py

# Or run individual experiments:
python experiments/exp01_baseline.py
python experiments/exp02_epsilon.py
python experiments/exp03_population.py
python experiments/exp04_clipping.py
```

### High-Level Python API Usage
```python
from private_llm_analytics.service.analytics import AnalyticsService

# Initialize from YAML configurations
service = AnalyticsService.from_config_dir("configs")

# Load parquet interaction telemetry (or generate synthetic)
service.load_data("data/interactions_n10k.parquet")

# Query User-Normalized Share for external recipient provider_a
result = service.compute(
    metric="user_normalized_share",
    recipient="provider_a",
    epsilon=1.0,
    delta=1e-6,
)

print(result["results"]["provider_distribution"])
```

